---
// /beats — Noun Beats. An installable mobile web app (PWA) about Nouns and beats:
// a 16-step, 7-track beat maker played by a band of Noun drummers, live pads,
// private rooms on the drum relay (bc-nb<CODE> party frames), a seeded daily
// challenge, and beats shared as a URL hash (/beats/#b=...). Its own app identity:
// /beats/manifest.webmanifest (id + scope /beats/) and /beats/sw.js (offline shell,
// runtime cache for noun.pics art). Human taps land on the town drum through
// POST /api/drum/signal (app "/beats"), one tap = one beat.
// v2 (2026-10-05): The Floor — seven always-on public rooms (bc-nbpub-<slug>) with
// house bands and a peak-groove meter, presence from GET /api/beats/floor; the Beat
// Wall (functions/api/beats.ts: publish, nod, remix); Moments — earned, numbered,
// holographic cards kept on the phone (serials from /api/beats/moment), shaped like
// TZIP-21 metadata but never minted; Media Session lock-screen controls.
// v1 built 2026-09-28, v2 2026-10-05, by Claude on briefs from Mike. Source of truth for
// the inline script/style lives in this file; no layout, no framework, no external
// requests besides noun.pics art, /api/drum* and /api/beats*.
---
